course: dictionary
lesson: 9196
title: Soft: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word soft can mean many things, so you need context to know which meaning is right. Read the words around it. «Blowing too hard makes a recorder jump up to a shrill squeal; a soft, steady breath gives a clear note.» Here soft means gentle, not forceful, because the clue is blowing too hard.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. «Teeth are brushed gently in small circles with a soft brush, because hard scrubbing hurts the gums.» Does not hard fit? Yes: the brush is not hard, so it does not hurt the gums. Soft means not hard here.
explain: The same word can also mean quiet or not bright. «A girl in Vermont walks carefully and throws soft snowballs at nobody's face.» Here soft means gentle, so the snowballs will not hurt anyone. Look at the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Soft can mean not hard or firm, like a soft pillow.
fact: Soft can mean smooth and nice to touch, like soft fur.
fact: Soft can mean quiet and gentle, like a soft voice, or «softly spoken».
fact: Soft can mean not bright, like soft light.
exercise: «Teeth are brushed gently in small circles with a soft brush, because hard scrubbing hurts the gums and wears the teeth.» In this sentence, what does soft mean? | Full of water | Very bright | *Not hard, so it does not hurt the gums | Very loud
exercise: Nadia orders a soft drink at the café. What is a soft drink? | *A drink without alcohol, such as a fizzy or sweet drink | A hot drink made with milk | A drink that is very hard to find | A drink you eat with a spoon
exercise: «A girl in Vermont throws soft snowballs at nobody's face.» What does soft suggest about the snowballs? | *Gentle, so they will not hurt | Dirty and wet | Loud and noisy | Icy and very hard
test: «The snailfish has soft bones and a watery body.» What does soft mean here? | *Not hard or firm | Very bright | Very loud | Kind to others
test: «She spoke softly so the baby would sleep.» What does softly mean? | Brightly | *Quietly and gently | Very loudly | Hard and firm
exam: «The soft light made the room feel calm.» What does soft mean here? | Hard and firm | *Not bright | Sweet to taste | Very loud
